  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. 4 booked studies; 3 cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) excluded, no orders.\n\n1) pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0001). NKDA, no premed. Diabetic (diet); last Cr 9/24 >30 days → pre-scan creatinine ordered (sr-t0008). New outside Cr 10/22 = 1.52 (eGFR 64) arrived mid-work: not AKI by policy definition (28 days apart, undocumented), eGFR ≥30 → no prophylaxis; decision left in place, repeat draw kept. Patient instructed + updated; follow-up task to Dr. Okafor.\n\n2) pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0002). 2019 radiology report grades iohexol reaction MODERATE (allergy-list \"anaphylaxis, patient report\" doesn't change grade) → prednisone 50 mg 20:00/02:00/08:00 (mr-t0005) + diphenhydramine 50 mg 08:00 (mr-t0006), needs driver. Corrected Cr 10/14 = 2.8 (original 0.98 was another patient's sample) → eGFR 24 → added NS 500 mL IV 08:00 (mr-t0017). Instructions sent in Spanish/English, then corrected message (arrive 07:45). Follow-up task for new reduced kidney function/allergy label.\n\n3) pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00 CT A/P w/ contrast (sr-t0003). AKI 10/04 not resolved, no later Cr → pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0009), NS 500 mL IV 12:00 (mr-t0007), metformin held (mr-00392, last dose 10/25 PM, ≥48 h after), recheck Cr ≥10/28 13:00 (sr-t0011) + restart-review task. Outside 2022 report received mid-work: MODERATE iopamidol reaction → added prednisone 50 mg 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0018) + diphenhydramine 12:00 (mr-t0019), driver; corrected message sent; allergy-list task (iopamidol not codable in catalog).\n\n4) pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00 CT A/P without contrast (sr-t0004), ordered as booked, no prep; patient told. Outside report of a mild iohexol reaction recorded on allergy list (alg-t0020); no change for non-contrast study.\n\nProgress notes written for each patient citing RBC-RAD-07; four new inbox items completed. Unrelated pre-existing inbox items were left untouched.",
